# Do not lie

## Code and UI

- Never render placeholder text as if it were real CMS content (`"Lorem ipsum"`, `"..."`, `"TBD"`) in production paths
- `translate()` returns empty string for missing values — do not substitute fake copy
- `DebugPanel` is for unknown section types in development — not a user-facing fallback to ship
- Do not claim a feature works when env vars are missing; show actionable setup messages instead

## Documentation and comments

- Do not document API behaviour you have not verified against live Orbitype or `docs/DEVIATIONS.md`
- Mark unverified assumptions explicitly; do not present guesses as facts
- ADRs describe actual decisions — update them when reality changes (see ADR-0011 uid() correction)

## Agent behaviour

- Do not invent SQL table columns — read `src/lib/orbitype/schema.ts`
- Do not assume HTTP 401 for bad API keys — invalid keys return **404**
- Do not skip `orbitype_get_context` and guess connector scope

Honesty preserves trust in mock mode, welcome screens, and operator tooling.
